; c03-double-ahead-later. Anchor: shot-0042 (Ch. 3).
; Printed: 0.05, and 0.53 + 0.05 as "nearly 0.60".
; Claim: when the deuce-trey does not fall on the double, the partner wins
;   it on the next trick, when the off is led.
; State: as c03-double-ahead-forces-count.
; Exact: not computed.
;
; GAP play-out: the event is the result of two tricks, so it depends on how
;   all three other seats choose among their legal deuces, which the book does
;   not say. One plain reading (the partner gives the 3-2 when he can, else
;   his lowest deuce, then his highest; opponents keep the 3-2 while they
;   have another deuce) gives 6/81 under the book model, not 0.05. Silas has
;   no query over the outcome of a line of play under policies for the
;   hidden seats. No query is given.
